---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rooms | Aura Homes"
  description="Beautiful second-life rooms that bring people back to nature, one room at a time."
  descriptor="Rooms"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">Rooms</p>
      <h1>A finished room.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">
        Beside the house, or a small stay on the property. Clear, mirrored, or tinted glass, and flat. The room sits on its steel frame in the grass. Two sides can open, and a panel can be the door.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <h2>What you are looking at</h2>
      <p>Honey oak, linen, and the meadow still in view when the long side opens. A desk can face the field. A bed can sit under a skylight. A wood-fired tub, when it is the point, has its own steel frame.</p>
      <p>The scroll film of that room plays on <a href="/">the opening page</a>. It is the same room, held low in the grass.</p>
      <h2>What comes after the room</h2>
      <p>Glass on piles, a deck, and a small resort are <a href="/customs">custom work</a>. A farm wall is a different long side of this same room. Water from the air comes later. The sequence is written in the <a href="/master-plan">master plan</a>.</p>
      <p>If the room is the one you want, <a href="/pre-order">hold a place</a>. The page takes no payment.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
